            <ArticleTitle>Role of Small Airways in Asthma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>473-82</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.iac.2016.03.009</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0889-8561(16)30009-1</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Asthma is an inflammatory condition of both the small and large airways. Recently the small airways have gained attention as studies have shown significant inflammation in the small airways in all severities of asthma. This inflammation has correlated with peripheral airway resistance and as a result, noninvasive methods to reliably measure small airways have been pursued. In addition, recent changes in asthma inhalers have led to alterations in drug formulations and the development of extrafine particle inhalers that improve delivery to the distal airways.</AbstractText>
